infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Sizing an aggregate: data graph vs invariant
  desc Small — sized by the invariant it enforces — is the right default
  compares
    - label Large aggregate (by data graph)
      children
        - label Bundle everything related
          desc Order owns every line item, shipment, payment, note
        - label Whole graph locked per write
          desc Unrelated operations serialize on one lock
        - label Cascade-loads the full graph
          desc Reads hydrate data the operation never touches
        - label Spanning invariant stays hidden
          desc "Everything about an Order" is not a rule
    - label Small aggregate (by invariant)
      children
        - label Smallest set the rule needs
          desc Quote + LineItems for the credit-limit invariant
        - label Locks only the invariant's data
          desc Independent aggregates commit in parallel
        - label Each aggregate loaded alone
          desc Others referenced by ID, no cascade
        - label Each rule visible in code
          desc Cross-aggregate sync via domain events, eventually
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
